# (build 105) The CRT page on the owner's Windows PC as tools/display_probe.c
# measured it (Windows, SDL 3.4.16, Direct3D 12 on an RTX 3080 Ti): the
# ASUS ProArt PA32UCX, 3840x2160 at 100% (pixel density 1), Windows's HDR
# off. Windowed at the game's 960x672: three display lines a scanline --
# scanlines yes, the grille wants fullscreen; fullscreen, nine: every mask,
# four-pixel triads. HDR: NO HDR, and PEAK's AUTO falls back to 1000. Then
# the probe again with Windows's "Use HDR" on: a headroom of 14.995 over an
# SDR white of 1.0 in scRGB (80 nits), so AUTO is 1200 nits -- the panel's
# rated peak. The words are the probe's PS2_DISPLAY lines. The route reads
# its own settings.json.
start new
wait screen title
display 960x672 full=3840x2160
press esc
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press c
expect crt scanlines ON
expect crt summary SCANLINES
press down
press c
expect crt mask APERTURE GRILLE / NEEDS FULLSCREEN
wait ticks 17
shot pa32ucx_window
display 3840x2160 fullscreen full=3840x2160
expect crt mask APERTURE GRILLE
press right
press right
expect crt mask SHADOW MASK
expect crt summary SHADOW MASK
press down
press down
press right
expect crt hdr ON / NO HDR
press c
expect crt peak AUTO 1000 NITS
wait ticks 6
shot pa32ucx_hdr_page
display 3840x2160 fullscreen full=3840x2160 hdr=14.995/1.000 sdr=80
expect crt hdr ON
expect crt peak AUTO 1200 NITS
wait ticks 16
shot pa32ucx_hdr_on
display 960x672 full=3840x2160 hdr=14.995/1.000 sdr=80
expect crt hdr ON
expect crt peak AUTO 1200 NITS
press b
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
